# DTF tier manifest: migration
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=nexus (the #2457 topology: a
# real Nexus 3 migration source next to the backend on the slot's network).
# Oracle: nexus bootstrap -> seed (single-arch AND multi-arch AND large-index
# fixtures) -> real AK migration -> vendored nexus_migrate_assert (assert.sh):
# non-zero-while-bug (config-blob 404, child-manifest 404, oci_blobs==0,
# per-image `docker pull`). The multi-arch leg is the one #2457/v1.5.5 missed
# and is exercised explicitly.
#
# #6195 / #6196 (window_dryrun.sh, artifact-keeper 1.12.3): a raw repository
# on the same Nexus is seeded in two batches. FIX #6195: a migration with
# date_from = the newest batch-A lastModified migrates only batch B (red on
# main: Nexus ignored the window and migrated all five). FIX #6196: after an
# unwindowed re-run, a dry run with conflict_resolution=skip reports all five
# as skipped, 0 completed, 0 bytes (red on main: 5 completed).
#
# #6519 (source_timestamps.sh, 1.13.0): FIX a migration with
# import_source_timestamps keeps each asset's Nexus blobCreated as created_at
# and records its lastDownloaded as one marker download (red on main: import
# time, no marker). GUARD an asset never downloaded gets no marker, and a
# migration without the flag keeps the import time.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives admin login + repeated OCI token
# exchanges + two `docker pull`s back-to-back through one admin user; matches
# the rig harness, which runs its pool slot the same way. (Base default stays
# ON; a tier that must disable a shipped control does so explicitly, §2.2.)
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.nexus"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
COVERS="6195 6196 6519"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
